I found a similar topic here :
Remove the duplicate characters in a string
The solution given by the author was that :
public static void removeDuplicates(char[] str) {
  if (str == null) return;
  int len = str.length;
  if (len < 2) return;

  int tail = 1;

  for (int i = 1; i < len; ++i) {
       int j;

       for (j = 0; j < tail; ++j) {
       if (str[i] == str[j]) break;
       }

       if (j == tail) {
       str[tail] = str[i];
       ++tail;
     }
  }
  str[tail] = 0;
 }
